{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"28f23b1c29684f7fc0c9a8fbac0f084a278c7745ea5c81d8b9d662fe9a127da6","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review plan-relation snapshot reducer","key_entities":["plan-relation-snapshot-error","rebar review-plan",".tickets-tracker","plan_relation_snapshot","_store/event_append._prepare_event","os.makedirs"],"problem_keywords":["empty ticket directory","plan-relation reducer","event-less tickets","INDETERMINATE verdict","store detritus"],"propositions":["A ticket directory with no CREATE or SNAPSHOT event causes the plan-relation reducer to error, failing unrelated ticket plan reviews with INDETERMINATE verdicts","Event-less directories are created by process death mid-write (makedirs before atomic rename completes) and persist invisibly in local clones since git cannot track empty directories","The reducer tolerates and warns on event-less directories instead of failing the snapshot, while maintaining strict error handling for genuinely corrupt tickets that hold events but fail to reduce","The writer does not remove the directory post-creation because cleanup is unsafe under concurrent multi-session store writes and cannot repair already-broken clones"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787308812434267001,"uuid":"d57440ff-b0b9-47a9-bbc0-bd8d52f4864f"}